From: SinceVIC20 <codedesk@v3biolab.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:35:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] dashboard: one full-height traffic graph, with the
 separate graphs a click away

The Traffic Graph widget shows one interface at a time on a single
full-height graph, in and out shaded on one shared scale. The scale fits
the traffic in steps, up at once and down a step at a time after a quiet
minute, or is logarithmic from 1 kb/s to the link speed; clicking the
scale or its Lin/Log button switches. Interface names across the top
select one, in an order set by dragging, a cog chooses which appear,
and arrows page through them when they don't all fit. A line down the
graph, with a dot where it crosses each curve, gives the rates shown in
the header. Buttons under the link switch back to the separate in and
out graphs and copy and save a picture. The choices are remembered in
the browser, and added, removed or renamed interfaces are picked up
when the dashboard regains focus.
